{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`rebar verify-opcert` is the op-cert merge gate. In `_gate` (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`), a ticket whose `rebar.show_ticket(...)` raised was skipped with `except Exception: continue`. A closed ticket whose state could not be reduced then dropped out of scope, so with `verify.require_environment` set the gate could print OK and exit 0 while that ticket had no valid certificate. A security gate must fail closed on data it cannot read. Found while fixing golden-busied-nag.\n\nTwo more ways a ticket escapes, found in review: tickets are enumerated only from the merged-log walk (`_collect_all`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py`), and a SNAPSHOT that folded unsigned events adds nothing to that walk (`_build_authorship_ledger` in `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` keeps signed events only); and a ticket can become closed through a CREATE (`data.status`, `process_create`) or an EDIT (`data.fields.status`), not only a STATUS event.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. When `show_ticket` raises, decide from the ticket's raw event files, read straight from its directory with `_active_event_files`. New helper `_may_be_closed(ticket_dir)` returns true when there is no event file, any file does not parse, any file is a SNAPSHOT (compacted history of unknown content), or any event can set `closed` (`_sets_closed`: STATUS `data.status`, CREATE `data.status`, EDIT `data.fields.status`). Only when it is false (every event parsed, no SNAPSHOT, nothing ever closed) is the ticket out of scope. The gate does not re-derive which branch of a forked STATUS chain the reducer keeps (smallest UUID, `process_status` in `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py`), since that reduce is what failed: a closed-then-reopened ticket that cannot be reduced is judged.\n2. A ticket that may be closed stays in scope with reason `unreadable ticket state (<ExceptionType>: <message>)` and is judged like any unsatisfied ticket: `_is_enforced` on the close anchor from `_close_anchor_event` (a missing anchor is enforced), failing the gate (exit 1) only when a required environment is set; advisory mode reports it and exits 0.\n3. New helper `_gate_ticket_ids(events, tracker)` enumerates the walk's tickets plus every ticket directory in the store, keeping the walk's exclusions (`_is_gate_exempt_ticket`, `_is_archived_ticket`), so a ticket the walk never yields is still considered.\n4. `_scoped_state` holds the try/except, so `_gate` does not grow in complexity.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nIn `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, with the remote-backed fixture, `rebar.show_ticket` monkeypatched to raise `RuntimeError` for one ticket, and `verify_opcert.cli` run in-process:\n- closed ticket with `--require-environment`: exit 1, reason `unreadable ticket state (RuntimeError: ...)`; advisory: exit 0, reported; `--since` after its close: `[grandfathered]`, exit 0;\n- closed then reopened ticket: judged, exit 1;\n- in-progress ticket plus a raw SNAPSHOT, an EDIT writing `status: closed`, or a CREATE born closed (parametrized): judged, exit 1;\n- a ticket directory holding only a SNAPSHOT (absent from the walk): enumerated and judged, exit 1;\n- in-progress ticket with STATUS events only, and a ticket with only an open CREATE: out of scope.\nThe closed, SNAPSHOT, EDIT, CREATE and walk-absent cases fail against the previous code. Then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With a required environment set, a closed ticket whose `show_ticket` raises makes `rebar verify-opcert` exit 1 and report `unreadable ticket state`: shown by a test that fails against `except Exception: continue`.\n- [ ] In advisory mode such a ticket is reported with exit 0; under `--since` past its close it is reported `[grandfathered]` with exit 0.\n- [ ] A raising ticket whose raw events include a SNAPSHOT, an EDIT or CREATE that sets `closed`, or any close in its history is judged; one whose parsed events never set `closed` and include no SNAPSHOT stays out of scope: shown by tests.\n- [ ] A ticket directory the merged-log walk does not yield is still enumerated: shown by `test_ticket_absent_from_the_walk_is_still_enumerated`.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795262296088276001,"uuid":"dcaf39c4-0138-42dc-a572-71d945971a73"}